# settings-audio: the real Ajustes window opened on the Audio group, over the
# real main screen. Same real path as the other settings fixtures
# (main_screen_action(ACTION_APP_SETTINGS) -> dialog_construct ->
# src/dialog_settings.c); the fixture then presses the "Audio" tab of the bottom
# bar (page 1, index 1), which calls settings_goto() to scroll the grid to the
# group and move the focus there. The group holds, in order, the "Line-in,
# Line-out" row, the "Play,Rec gain" row (the two sliders this fixture is
# about), "Audio enhance", SP mode and the voice rows.
#
# Geometry of the row it measures: the label sits in grid column 0 and the two
# sliders in two 3-column cells, each with the value label to its right (the
# 159 px wide slider and the "+3.0"/"-4.0" label it prints). The two sliders look
# identical on purpose: what tells them apart is the parameter behind each one,
# which is why the fixture gives them different values (see below) and then
# drags the Rec one.
#
# Play/rec gains: distinct, non-zero, so the two sliders of the row can be told
# apart in the render (each one shows its own value) and so a slider that moves
# the *other* one is visible. The radio loads them from params.db
# (src/params/params.c, params_load_float); the fixture sets the same field.
# With the callback of Rec gain wired to the output function -the copy/paste of
# issue #26- this fixture stops the run (see scenario_settle in src/screens.c).
#
# Deterministic: the date/time fields read the harness' fixed clock, not the
# host's (tools/ui_harness/CMakeLists.txt links with `--wrap=time`).

name settings-audio
screen settings-audio

seed 20

play_gain_db 3
rec_gain_db -4

frequency_hz 14074000
tx_frequency_hz 14074000
fft_width_hz 384000

mode usb
vfo A
agc auto

split false
att false
pre false
atu false
ant 1

smeter_db -73

battery_v 12.1
external_v 13.8
battery_cap 76
charging false

rxtx rx
